{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'cat /workspace/TASK.md'","aggregated_output":"# Task: H02 — Batch slot allocator: explicit status result instead of a single bool\n\n> Held-out RFC-0005 suite · Shape: Localized API evolution (2/2).\n> You are maintaining an **existing correct system**; do not rewrite it from\n> scratch. Change only what the task requires.\n\n## Base (workspace)\n\nThe workspace contains a correct, deterministic batch slot-allocator program.\nIt evaluates whether a request for `amount` units fits into a named slot\n(slot must exist, and its free capacity `capacity - used` must be at least\n`amount`). The evaluation function currently returns **a single bool**:\n`true` when the claim would fit, `false` otherwise — with no distinction\nbetween \"unknown slot\", \"insufficient capacity\", or \"invalid request\".\nTwo call sites in the same module consume that function (one maps a batch of\nrequests to outcome labels, one reports capacity).\n\nThe program is driven by the environment variable `H02_SCENARIO` (scenario\nname) and prints deterministic lines. There is no persistence, no network, and\nno wall-clock dependency.\n\n## Required change\n\nChange the return contract of the evaluation function from a single bool to an\n**explicit status result** that distinguishes failure classes:\n\n1. Claim would fit → success (the evaluated slot).\n2. `amount < 1` → explicit error whose text is exactly `E_H02_INVALID_AMOUNT`.\n3. Slot does not exist → explicit error `E_H02_NOT_FOUND`.\n4. Slot exists but free capacity is insufficient → explicit error\n   `E_H02_CAPACITY`.\n\nEvery existing call site must consume the new result and **preserve the error\ncontent** (no class may be silently folded into a generic \"deny\"). A request\nthat fits must still be reported the same way as before; the capacity report\nbehavior must not change.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe hidden verifier builds the project and drives the compiled program through\nscenarios via `H02_SCENARIO`, then checks the exact output lines. It covers:\n\n- preserved success behavior and the capacity report;\n- explicit classification of insufficient capacity (recoverable error);\n- explicit classification of an unknown slot;\n- explicit classification of a zero/negative amount (fatal caller error);\n- error content preserved through the request-mapping call site.\n\nThe workspace exposes only the program state and this task; the verifier is\nnot visible to you.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
